referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Judge"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/5005052"} "Bernhard Gaber"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Judge"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/5005053"} "Alwin Seifert"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "A total of 94 works by 58 architects or architectural firms, with a total of 87 participants from 14 countries, were submitted for the two categories, “" [:a {:href "/results/920042"} "Town Planning"] "” and “Architectural Designs”. The jury finally accepted 82 works for the competitions. The remaining projects were exhibited “hors concours”. The exhibits for the two competitions, “" [:a {:href "/results/920042"} "Town Planning"] "” and “Architectural Designs” were identical, but were assessed separately for both categories. Therefore, works that were not awarded with a medal " [:a {:href "/results/920044"} "cannot be attributed to either category"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In addition to the members listed above, Cultural officer Oswald Bieber (1874/1876-1955) and the future Minister of Armaments and War Production Albert Speer (1905-1981) were supposed to be members of the jury, according to the exhibition catalog, but were not  listed in the final " [:strong {} "Official Report"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Himself a regular cross country skier, " [:a {:href "/athletes/920042"} "Hermann Kutschera"] " submitted a design for a " [:em {} "Ski (Jumping) Stadium"] " to the Olympic art contests. It earned a gold medal, but was never built, the plans being lost during World War II. The German " [:a {:href "/athletes/920672"} "Werner March"] " won a silver medal with the same entry that had earned him and his brother a gold medal in the town planning event. Third place went to an Austria duo, " [:a {:href "/athletes/920086"} "Hermann Stiegholzer"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/920036"} "Herbert Kastinger"] ", designing an " [:em {} "Arena for car, bicycle and equestrian sports in Vienna"] "."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Catalogue Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Translated Title"] [:th {} "Original Title"] [:th {} "Title in Olympic Report or Catalogue"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "439"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/920042"} "Hermann Kutschera"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUT"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUT.png"}] "AUT"]] [:td {} "Ski Stadium"] [:td {} "Ski-Stadion"] [:td {} "Ski-Stadion. 1936"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "68"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/920672"} "Werner March"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "Reichssportfeld"] [:td {} "Reichssportfeld"] [:td {} "Reichssportfeld. 1935"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {} [:a {:class "footnote", :href "#", :title "His brother Walter March is not mentioned for this project.", :data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right"} "1"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "442"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/920036"} "Herbert Kastinger"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/920086"} "Hermann Stiegholzer"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUT"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3